  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_025 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) is the clear best at 0.678 acc / 0.646 F1 and also the cheapest (5.90 GPU-h). The RNA encoder switch from pca_n2000→scvi_n200 gave a large +0.039 boost, while the image encoder swap (resnet50→imagenet_vit_l) with pca_n2000 was roughly neutral (0.639 vs 0.635). Question: does a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) interact beneficially with the scvi_n200 RNA encoder, where the representation is richer and may complement a more powerful visual backbone? This experiment (config_018) is a single-variable change from config_025 (resnet50→imagenet_vit_l), keeping everything else fixed, so any accuracy shift is cleanly attributable to the image encoder. It is the best use of experiment 4 because it directly extends the most promising direction, costs a moderate ~6–7 GPU hours (comparable to config_006's 7.02), and if it improves accuracy it identifies a new best baseline to further exploit in the remaining 6 experiments; if it does not, it confirms resnet50 suffices and we can pivot to aggregation/fusion changes next."
}

